  "Question": "The value of \\(\\dfrac3{a+b}\\) when \\(a=4\\) and \\(b=-4\\) is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac38\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "any finite number",
    "E": "meaningless"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "A fraction is defined only when its denominator is nonzero. Substituting the given values gives\n\\[\na+b=4+(-4)=0.\n\\]\nThe expression would therefore be \\(3/0\\). This is undefined because no number multiplied by \\(0\\) can equal \\(3\\). The answer is “meaningless,” choice E.",
